  "id": "idioretinal-light",
  "term": "idioretinal light",
  "definition": "Idioretinal light is the faint, cloudy gray patches seen in the visual field when the eyes are not being stimulated and no after-images are present. In this historical usage, it refers to a visual phenomenon considered important in older theories of after-images.",
